  "sourceChanges": [
    {
      "file": "proj/src/game.c",
      "originalSha256": "80d2f5184a0ef23c866f439dba1f0ef312eb068e8f7bc65528e2729eb9ff9c16",
      "patchedSha256": "e6bbd30754ed531ed39ff9f1890a0d0529b94cab6a9c4f7cfdee4761a1775281",
      "reason": "An enemy collision calls end_game and frees the round character, then original Game Over Escape calls end_game a second time. Actual complete owning event-handler/sprite lifecycle RED detects the same allocation freed twice. Make round cleanup idempotent, clear the released character pointer and record a score only once. Actual constructor/collision/Exit sequence GREEN; no emulator adaptation or asset changes."
    },
    {
      "file": "proj/src/text.c",
      "originalSha256": "d95624d33b1818f74aa65201210cab341b1ae1af77d3a7ff052c9b4c232d3a96",
      "patchedSha256": "c23b2bb6ee528872edcfd055c3a135e0a5b2b248c198a2f7be7eb8d37767c243",
      "reason": "Original free_numbers iterates0 through10 over a ten-entry bitmap array. Actual ARM64 GameOver Escape aborts freeing0x800000005 from the adjacent GAME_STATE/nextglobal, and extracted APK unrolls the eleventh pointer read. Actual owning text cleanup plus bitmap destructor regression RED rejects the eleventh foreign free; GREEN releases exactly ten pixel-buffer/metadata pairs through existing deleteBitmap. Keep source assets and gameplay unchanged."
    }
  ],
